{
    "_comment": [
        "Custom vendor VHAL properties for SmartAAOS.",
        "",
        "Installed to /vendor/etc/automotive/vhalconfig/ - the reference VHAL",
        "loads every .json file in that directory at startup, so a new property",
        "needs no C++ and no rebuild of the HAL.",
        "",
        "Property IDs are bit fields: group | area | type | unique id.",
        "  0x20000000 VENDOR group (an OEM's own namespace)",
        "  0x01000000 GLOBAL area (not per-seat or per-door)",
        "  0x00400000 INT32, 0x00600000 FLOAT, 0x00100000 STRING",
        "",
        "The stock config files use C++ enum names such as",
        "TestVendorProperty::MIXED_TYPE_PROPERTY_FOR_TEST. Those only resolve",
        "for names compiled into the VHAL, so a genuinely new property has to",
        "use the raw numeric ID. The loader accepts that."
    ],
    "properties": [
        {
            "_name": "VENDOR_DRIVE_MODE  0x21400001  INT32, writable",
            "property": 557842433,
            "defaultValue": { "int32Values": [1] },
            "access": "VehiclePropertyAccess::READ_WRITE",
            "changeMode": "VehiclePropertyChangeMode::ON_CHANGE"
        },
        {
            "_name": "VENDOR_SERVICE_DUE_KM  0x21600002  FLOAT, read only",
            "property": 559939586,
            "defaultValue": { "floatValues": [7500.0] },
            "access": "VehiclePropertyAccess::READ",
            "changeMode": "VehiclePropertyChangeMode::ON_CHANGE"
        },
        {
            "_name": "VENDOR_BATTERY_HEALTH  0x21100003  STRING, read only",
            "property": 554696707,
            "defaultValue": { "stringValue": "GOOD" },
            "access": "VehiclePropertyAccess::READ",
            "changeMode": "VehiclePropertyChangeMode::STATIC"
        }
    ]
}
